  "facts": [
    "The Arthur Kill Vertical Lift Bridge, opened in 1959, boasts the world’s longest lift span, with 215‑foot towers and a 558‑foot truss that creates a 500‑foot channel for ships.",
    "After a 16‑year hiatus, the bridge was rehabilitated in 2006, painted royal blue in homage to its B&O heritage, and resumed freight service, now moving garbage and freight across Staten Island.",
    "U.S. Coast Guard rules cap the bridge’s lowering to just two 15‑minute windows daily, a restriction that keeps the channel open for shipping while still allowing essential rail traffic."
